@page "/tables/simple-table/rows/context-menu"

@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.Shared.Enums
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.Shared.Models
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.SimpleTable.Components
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.SimpleTable.Components.Columns

<h3>Row Context Menu</h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    Right-clicking a row raises <code>RowContextMenuRequested</code> with the row's item and the mouse position, and
    that is all the table does — it opens no menu, builds no menu context and filters no entries. The handler
    is the bridge: it decides which rows the menu is about, which entries apply to them, and sends its own
    <code>IContextMenuContext</code> down the ordinary context-menu pipeline.
</DescriptionBanner>

<DescriptionBanner>
    Right-clicking a row outside the selection replaces the selection with that row, so the highlight and the
    menu always agree on what an action would apply to. Right-clicking inside the selection leaves it alone
    and the menu acts on all of it. The table does none of this — the handler below does.
</DescriptionBanner>

<DescriptionBanner>
    <code>Split into batches</code> is declared <code>ApplicableTo</code> high-quantity rows only, so it shows
    while every selected row has a <code>Quantity</code> of 100 or more and hides as soon as one does not. The
    handler states what was clicked, each entry states what it can handle, and the menu shows the entries that
    cover everything clicked.
</DescriptionBanner>

<DescriptionBanner>
    Suppression covers the whole row, cell content included. The <code>Note</code> column opts back out with
    <code>@@oncontextmenu:stopPropagation="true"</code>, so right-clicking inside its input gives the browser's
    own menu — cut, copy, paste — while the rest of the row still opens the custom one.
</DescriptionBanner>

@if (_lastAction is not null)
{
    <p>Last action: <code>@_lastAction</code></p>
}

<SimpleTable Items="s_items"
             SelectionMode="SelectionMode.Multiple"
             @bind-SelectedItems="_selectedItems"
             RowContextMenuRequested="@((RowContextMenuEventArgs<ExampleTableItem> args) => RowRightClickAsync(args))"
             MaximumHeight="300px">
    <Columns>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Key" Title="Key">
            <CellContent>@context.Key</CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Value" Title="Value">
            <CellContent>@context.Value</CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Quantity" Title="Quantity">
            <CellContent>@context.Quantity</CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Note" Title="Note">
            <CellContent>
                <input class="native-context-menu-input" value="@context.Value" @oncontextmenu:stopPropagation="true" />
            </CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
    </Columns>
</SimpleTable>

<SampleContextMenu ActionInvoked="@(action => _lastAction = action)" />
